# .claude/devil/critical-globs.conf — the project's critical-path scope.
#
# One glob per line, matched (shell `case` pattern) against repo-relative
# changed-file paths. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# This file is DATA — it is read and matched, never executed.
#
# Consumers (kept in agreement by construction — both read THIS file):
#   .claude/scripts/devil.sh              escalates codex reasoning effort and
#                                         injects critical-invariants.md when a
#                                         diff touches a matching path
#   .claude/hooks/critical-path-tripwire.sh  scopes the authoring-time tripwire
#
# Match whole modules generously — harmless extra hits are cheaper than a
# missed critical file. Equality between consumers is guaranteed; COVERAGE is
# not: add an anchor-based completeness check for that
# (selftest/critical-globs-completeness.sh is the skeleton).
#
# Copy this file to critical-globs.conf (drop the .example) and edit.
# Examples for a payments-style service:
#*src/billing/*
#*src/payments/*
#*src/wallet/*
#*src/common/money/*
